  "subtitle": "[ASSET: left | SpankinOfYourLife | width=12%] [ASSET: right | HeMeantIt | width=14%] This month's VMA goes to [LINK:1964:FF_28|FF #28|2027-07-30] where Ben Grimm says to Marvel Girl, \"If you weren't a <i>female</i>, I'd <i>demolish</i> ya!&nbsp; But the only thing I can do to a nut like <i>you</i> is give ya the spankin' of your life!\"\n[BR]\n[BR] And I guess he actually <i>meant</i> it!&nbsp; <i>Wow!</i>",
  "review_text": "Eight graded stories spread over 7 books (<i>Strange Tales</i> again with two) with a final weighted average of\n\n[SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx],\n\nwhich was over a half-point better than last month's <b>x.xx</b>.&nbsp; Were it not for this month's horrendous <i>Strange Tales</i>, it would certainly have come out better.\n\nHighlights of the month were definitely the three crossover books (four if you include the Thing's appearance in <i>Daredevil</i>, though the two did not actually cross paths) and of course the introduction of the Green Goblin.&nbsp; But the crossovers are the novelty here, even if sometimes clumsily pulled off.&nbsp; Marvel is making it <i>crystal</i> clear to the fans that they can expect to see characters appear regularly in each other's books, which I'm sure was a fantastic state of affairs for the readers of the day.&nbsp; Even the <i>villains</i> are now getting into the act, as is demonstrated with the Electro appearance in DD's mag.&nbsp; This has happened before, mind you (e.g. Human Torch vs Sandman, Spider-Man vs Dr. Doom), but it seems to be accelerating now.\n\nThe ratings may seem harsh in some places, but I'm keeping things in perspective, as I know there are <i>many</i> better stories that follow in the months to come.\n\n\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***8 graded stories over 7 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.08 grade character issue    weight 7.0   asm       ASM #14  1.00 6.0   iron      TOS #55  0.75 5.5   ff        FF #28   1.00 5.0   thor      JIM #105 0.75 5.0   giant     TTA #57  0.75 4.0   dd        DD #2    1.00 2.0   torch     ST #122  0.50 1.5   strange   ST #122  0.334.93*** LAST MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.58 grade character issue    weight 6.0   asm       ASM #13  1.00 6.0   ff        FF #27   1.00 6.0   iron      TOS #54  0.50 5.5   thor      JIM #104 0.50 5.5   xmen      XMEN #5  1.00 2.5   aven      AVEN #5  1.00 2.0   strange   ST #121  0.33 1.8   giant     TTA #56  0.75 1.8   torch     ST #121  0.504.35\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nGreen Goblin | villain | Milestone: (first)\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * Write something\n[HANG0] * Write something\n[HANG0] * Write something\n[HANG0] * Write something\n[HANG0] * Write something\n[HANG0] * Fourteen pages spent featuring the Human Torch against Dr. Doom's three discarded henchmen only reinforced the notion that I was perfectly happy not knowing what became of them.\n[HANG0] * A \"Nightmare\" of a villain wanted Dr. Strange asleep, but it was the comic that nearly got its wish.\n[HANG0] * Write something\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "[HANG0] * A new/old villain and his cohorts are set to plague the Avengers\n[HANG0] * It's more brute strength and slithering action for Thor\n[HANG0] * A towering figure... against <i>Giant-Man</i>?\n[HANG0] * Sub-Mariner mixes it up against the X-Men\n[HANG0] * A new villain tries to \"hunt\" down Spider-Man\n[HANG0] * The Fantastic Four head out to Yancy Street... where they are \"watched!\"\n[HANG0] * A new, suction-cupped menace faces the Human Torch\n[HANG0] * Dr. Strange takes on... <i>Loki</i>?&nbsp; (Can Thor be far away?)\n[HANG0] * And yet <i>another </i>new menace awaits Iron Man\n\nLooks like \"new villain month\" to me!\n\nAnd <i>boy!</i>  Though neither the Hulk nor the Sub-Mariner have their own books, Marvel sure has been parading them about in the pages of the various magazines.&nbsp; Subby is <i>obviously</i> set to appear in the X-Men, and I see Hulk's head on the cover of the <i>Avengers</i> book for next month, but does he <i>actually</i> appear?&nbsp; And if not, could this actually be a Hulk-free month?\n\nWe'll soon see!"
}